-- title:
--   The Frobenius-fixed special Picard group at $3$ has no $2$-torsion
-- statement:
--   Let $D_3$ be a level-$25$ reduction datum at $3$, let $Pic^0_{D_3}$ be the degree-zero Picard group of the special fiber, and let $Pic^0_{D_3}{}^{Fr=1}$ be its Frobenius-fixed subgroup. If $z$ belongs to this fixed subgroup and $2z=0$, then
--
--   $$z=0.$$
--
--   This is the special-fiber torsion exclusion used to prove oddness of the rational Jacobian subgroup.
-- source:
--   B. Mazur, Modular curves and the Eisenstein ideal, Publ. IHES 47 (1977); Lean formalization of the order-25 case for this mission. Modules in the MazurProof/Keystone/Tate families are adapted from anthropics/fermats-last-theorem (Apache-2.0) via the xiangyazi24/FLT fork.

